<title>CANADA: CHC Helicopter in extended North Sea deal.</title>
<headline>CHC Helicopter in extended North Sea deal.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOHN'S, Newfoundland 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>CHC Helicopter Corp said on Thursday that its British operating arm, British International, has won a three-year contract plus two further one-year renewal options, from Enterprise Oil Plc.</p>
<p>It gave no financial details of the deal, which is an extension of the current contract with Enterprise.</p>
<p>British International will use a combination of AS332L Super Pumas and Sikorsky S-61N and S76A+ helicopters from its base in Aberdeen, Scotland.</p>
<p>CHC said it operates 200 helicopters worldwide and has 1,600 employees.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100</p>
</text>
